{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_precision_is_negative_four_body_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_precision_is_negative_four_body_channel","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L57-L69","doc":"**Capstone — A=4 precision is a NEGATIVE leading-order 4-body saturation channel.** The baseline\novershoots (`a4_baseline_overshoots`), the 3-body clusters worsen it (`a4_three_body_makes_worse`), the\nrequired channel is negative (`a4_required_channel_negative`) and large (`a4_four_body_dominates`), and\nit is order-separated from 3-body higher orders (`a4_higher_order_ruled_out`). So A=3 (+small 3-body)\nand A=4 (−large 4-body) are opposite-sign regimes needing distinct leading channels — the μ₄ Δ_λ\nobject, open. scope-(a); no fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.mu4_more_fragile_than_mu3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.mu4_more_fragile_than_mu3","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L52-L55","doc":"**μ₄ is even more frame-fragile than μ₃**: its baseline-class spread `|μ₄^max|/|μ₄^min| =\n4.591/2.220 > 2` exceeds μ₃'s 1.73×. Report A=4 precision on the frame-independent physical ratio, not\nthe μ₄ residual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_four_body_dominates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_four_body_dominates","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L48-L50","doc":"**The 4-body channel dominates the 3-body cluster** by an order of magnitude:\n`|c₄|/c₃ = 3.89597/0.297 > 13`. The saturation term is large where the binding cluster is small. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_higher_order_ruled_out","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_higher_order_ruled_out","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L42-L46","doc":"**Order-separation.** The bounded (`|aₖ| ≤ 2`) 3-body higher-order tail `4·c₃·2·h²/(1−h²)` (`h² =\n0.0437062`) is `< 0.11`, ≪ the required `|c₄| ≈ 3.896`. So the A=4 miss is NOT closable by 3-body\nhigher orders — it needs a new leading 4-body channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_required_channel_negative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_required_channel_negative","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L38-L40","doc":"**The required 4-body channel is NEGATIVE** (the α-cluster saturation):\n`c₄ = ρ_strong(4) − (ρ_grad_G(4) + 4·c₃) < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_three_body_makes_worse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_three_body_makes_worse","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L33-L36","doc":"**The (positive) 3-body clusters make A=4 worse.** `ρ_grad_G(4) + 4·c₃ = 16.928` overshoots the\nphysical ratio `13.0316` even more than the baseline alone — so the missing piece cannot be a 3-body\ncontribution; it must be a distinct 4-body channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_baseline_overshoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.a4_baseline_overshoots","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A4PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L29-L31","doc":"**The A=4 graded baseline OVERSHOOTS** (`ρ_grad_G(4)/ρ_strong(4) > 1.2`, +20.8%) — the opposite of\nA=3, where it undershoots. The correction the data needs at A=4 is therefore NEGATIVE. ","signatureChunk":0}]}